r statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x+6)=f((x+3)+3)=f(x+3)=f(x),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is true by definition of the periodic extension.\n\n- Statement III is false. For example, take $x=2.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2+1)=f(3)=F(3)=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2)=F(2)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330780 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330781 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330782 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330783 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330784 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1041 "selection" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330784 13194139535092 true] [17592186330779 1110 #uuid "5b118759-5210-526c-a6c2-c0a1dddaa979" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330780 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330780 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330780 1111 #uuid "61d142cc-e17c-5323-a3f5-444bbea74b94" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330781 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330781 1111 #uuid "a22528d6-a9bc-52a9-a65a-11f2a13fb688" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330782 1034 "I only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330782 1111 #uuid "2bfff76c-6f49-5425-97a8-6ed0aba0c519" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330783 1034 "III only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330783 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330783 1111 #uuid "6d8c71c0-ac8d-51aa-ab1c-850eccdf1e39" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330784 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330784 1103 #edb/