3 #uuid "e05d9234-b5df-5b04-8082-fca6a02fdae1" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330883 1145 "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(0-0)-\\frac{1}{16}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330885 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330886 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330887 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330888 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330889 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1041 "field-1" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330888 13194139535092 true] [17592186330884 1110 #uuid "c6b9df2f-46a6-5e16-92ef-d7113796a1f4" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330885 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535092 true] [17592186330885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535092 true] [17592186330885 1111 #uuid "4185591d-cf23-56fb-97ac-67cc6af5b0c7" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330886 1034 "1" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535092 true] [1759218633088