atorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." 13194139535092 true] [17592186330893 1113 #uuid "bf13831d-c995-5cd8-9588-b47dc713d664" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330893 1145 "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-7\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(-1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330895 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330896 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330897 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330898 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330899 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1041 "field-1" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330898 13194139535092 true] [17592186330894 1110 #uuid "0fd06ea0-0027-5d72-bdf0-28d570b345bb" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330895 1034 "\\pi " 13194139535092 true] [17592186330895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045