be40-3136be85f39e" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330910 1145 "Since $f$ is the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F,$ we have  \n\n- $f(x+2\\pi )=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,2\\pi ).$\n\nWith that in mind, we examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We have\n\n$$\nf(x+4\\pi )=f((x+2\\pi )+2\\pi )=f(x+2\\pi )=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, take $x=2\\pi .$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2\\pi ) & =f(0+2\\pi )=f(0)=F(0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\nF(2\\pi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)\\ne F(x)$ for $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. This is exactly the definition of $2\\pi $-periodicity: \n\n$$\nf(x+2\\pi )=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330912 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330913 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330914 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330915 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330916 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1041 "selection" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330913 13194139535092 true] [17592186330911 1110 #uuid "1c115180-46e9-59de-95cf-762152a976ec" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330912 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330912 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330912 1111 #uuid "50da47be-a0ba-557d-bade-5daf37744529" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330913 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330913 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535092 true] [17592186330913 1111 #uuid "f801b0bd-2625-592b-b995-d97db5cacc07" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330914 1034 "III only" 13194139535092 true] [17592186330914 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 